# Newsletter Sign-up Implementation

Below is a complete, production-ready implementation covering the database schema, backend routes (Node.js/Express), and a frontend form. I'll note the key requirements as I go.

## 1. Database Schema (PostgreSQL)

```sql
CREATE TABLE subscribers (
  id            SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
  email         TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
  -- Store normalized (lowercased, trimmed) email for lookups
  email_normalized TEXT GENERATED ALWAYS AS (lower(trim(email))) STORED,
  consent_given BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
  consent_at    TIMESTAMPTZ,
  -- Double opt-in fields (recommended for GDPR)
  confirmed     BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE,
  confirm_token TEXT,
  confirm_token_expires TIMESTAMPTZ,
  -- Unsubscribe token (long-lived, unguessable)
  unsubscribe_token TEXT NOT NULL,
  unsubscribed_at   TIMESTAMPTZ,
  created_at        TIMESTAMPTZ NOT NULL DEFAULT now()
);

CREATE UNIQUE INDEX subscribers_email_norm_idx ON subscribers (email_normalized);
CREATE INDEX subscribers_unsub_token_idx ON subscribers (unsubscribe_token);
```

**Why these fields:**
- `consent_given` + `consent_at` prove **active, unforced consent** (requirement 3).
- `unsubscribe_token` enables **token-based unsubscribe** without login (requirement 2).
- `confirmed` supports double opt-in — strongly recommended for compliance (GDPR/ePrivacy/CAN-SPAM best practice).
- `unsubscribed_at` keeps the record for audit but stops all sending.

## 2. Backend (Node.js + Express)

```js
// newsletter.js
import express from 'express';
import crypto from 'node:crypto';
import validator from 'validator';
import rateLimit from 'express-rate-limit';
import { pool } from './db.js';          // pg Pool
import { sendMail } from './mailer.js';  // your mail provider

const router = express.Router();

// Throttle signups & unsubscribes per IP
router.use(rateLimit({ windowMs: 60_000, max: 10 }));

const SITE_URL = process.env.SITE_URL; // e.g. https://example.com
const TOKEN_TTL_MS = 1000 * 60 * 60 * 24; // 24h for confirmation

function newToken() {
  return crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('base64url');
}

/* ---------- SIGN-UP ---------- */
router.post('/api/newsletter/subscribe', async (req, res) => {
  const rawEmail = typeof req.body?.email === 'string' ? req.body.email : '';
  const consent = req.body?.consent === true || req.body?.consent === 'on';

  // ---- Server-side email validation ----
  const email = rawEmail.trim();
  if (!validator.isEmail(email, { allow_utf8_local_part: false })) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Please enter a valid email address.' });
  }
  if (email.length > 254) {
    return res.status(400).json({ error: 'Email address is too long.' });
  }

  // ---- Enforce active consent ----
  if (!consent) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      error: 'You must agree to receive the newsletter before subscribing.',
    });
  }

  const confirmToken = newToken();
  const unsubToken   = newToken();
  const expires      = new Date(Date.now() + TOKEN_TTL_MS);

  try {
    // Upsert: if they previously unsubscribed, allow them to re-subscribe
    const { rows } = await pool.query(
      `INSERT INTO subscribers
         (email, consent_given, consent_at, confirmed,
          confirm_token, confirm_token_expires, unsubscribe_token)
       VALUES ($1, TRUE, now(), FALSE, $2, $3, $4)
       ON CONFLICT (email_normalized) DO UPDATE
         SET consent_given          = TRUE,
             consent_at             = now(),
             confirmed              = FALSE,
             confirm_token          = EXCLUDED.confirm_token,
             confirm_token_expires  = EXCLUDED.confirm_token_expires,
             unsubscribed_at        = NULL
         WHERE subscribers.confirmed = FALSE
            OR subscribers.unsubscribed_at IS NOT NULL
       RETURNING id, email, confirmed`,
      [email, confirmToken, expires, unsubToken]
    );

    if (rows.length === 0) {
      // Already an active subscriber — don't leak that fact
      return res.json({ ok: true, message: 'Please check your inbox to confirm.' });
    }

    const confirmUrl =
      `${SITE_URL}/api/newsletter/confirm?token=${encodeURIComponent(confirmToken)}`;

    await sendMail({
      to: email,
      subject: 'Please confirm your newsletter subscription',
      text: `Click to confirm: ${confirmUrl}\n\nIf you didn't sign up, ignore this email.`,
    });

    return res.json({ ok: true, message: 'Please check your inbox to confirm.' });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('subscribe error', err);
    return res.status(500).json({ error: 'Something went wrong. Please try again.' });
  }
});

/* ---------- CONFIRM (double opt-in) ---------- */
router.get('/api/newsletter/confirm', async (req, res) => {
  const token = String(req.query.token || '');
  if (!token) return res.status(400).send('Invalid link.');

  await pool.query(
    `UPDATE subscribers
        SET confirmed = TRUE,
            confirm_token = NULL,
            confirm_token_expires = NULL
      WHERE confirm_token = $1
        AND confirmed = FALSE
        AND confirm_token_expires > now()
        AND unsubscribed_at IS NULL`,
    [token]
  );

  // Always show the same page; don't reveal token validity
  res.redirect('/newsletter/confirmed.html');
});

/* ---------- UNSUBSCRIBE ---------- */
router.get('/api/newsletter/unsubscribe', async (req, res) => {
  const token = String(req.query.token || '');
  if (!token) return res.status(400).send('Invalid link.');

  await pool.query(
    `UPDATE subscribers
        SET unsubscribed_at = now(), confirmed = FALSE
      WHERE unsubscribe_token = $1`,
    [token]
  );

  res.redirect('/newsletter/unsubscribed.html');
});

export default router;
```

Add `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`, HTTPS-only cookies, and HTTPS redirects at the proxy layer. The `unsubscribe_token` is used (not the ID) so links can't be enumerated.

**Include the unsubscribe link in every email** (CAN-SPAM / GDPR require this):

```text
Unsubscribe: ${SITE_URL}/api/newsletter/unsubscribe?token=${row.unsubscribe_token}
```
Also support `List-Unsubscribe: <https://example.com/api/newsletter/unsubscribe?token=...>` and `List-Unsubscribe-Post: List-Unsubscribe=One-Click` headers for one-click unsubscribe in mail clients.

## 3. Frontend Form

```html
<form id="newsletter-form" novalidate>
  <label for="nl-email">Email address</label>
  <input
    type="email"
    id="nl-email"
    name="email"
    autocomplete="email"
    required
    maxlength="254"
  />

  <!-- NOTE: NO 'checked' attribute — consent must be an active action -->
  <label class="consent">
    <input type="checkbox" id="nl-consent" name="consent" required />
    I agree to receive the newsletter. I can unsubscribe at any time.
  </label>

  <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>

  <p id="nl-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
</form>

<script>
  const form = document.getElementById('newsletter-form');
  const status = document.getElementById('nl-status');

  form.addEventListener('submit', async (e) => {
    e.preventDefault();
    status.textContent = '';

    const email   = document.getElementById('nl-email').value.trim();
    const consent = document.getElementById('nl-consent').checked;

    if (!email) { status.textContent = 'Please enter your email.'; return; }
    if (!consent) {
      status.textContent = 'Please tick the consent box to continue.';
      return;
    }

    const btn = form.querySelector('button');
    btn.disabled = true;

    try {
      const res = await fetch('/api/newsletter/subscribe', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
        body: JSON.stringify({ email, consent }),
      });
      const data = await res.json();
      status.textContent = data.error || data.message || 'Thanks!';
      if (res.ok) form.reset();
    } catch {
      status.textContent = 'Network error. Please try again.';
    } finally {
      btn.disabled = false;
    }
  });
</script>
```

## 4. How Each Requirement Is Met

| Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|
| **Server validates email** | `validator.isEmail()` + length check run on the server before any DB write; unique index prevents duplicates. The client-side `type="email"` is convenience only — never trusted. |
| **Subscribers can unsubscribe** | Every email carries a signed, unguessable `unsubscribe_token` link (`GET /api/newsletter/unsubscribe`). Works without login, updates `unsubscribed_at`, and stops all sends. |
| **Active consent, not pre-checked** | The checkbox has **no `checked` attribute**; the server rejects requests unless `consent === true`. `consent_given` + `consent_at` are recorded for audit. |

## 5. Recommended Extras

- **Double opt-in** (already wired above): don't send marketing mail until `confirmed = TRUE`. This proves consent and drastically reduces abuse.
- **Privacy notice link** next to the consent checkbox (required by GDPR).
- **Transactional emails only** vs. marketing — keep this list separate from system emails.
- **Bounce/complaint handling** — on hard bounce or spam complaint, set `unsubscribed_at`.
- **Don't distinguish "already subscribed"** in responses (avoids email enumeration).
- **Rate-limit** the subscribe endpoint (shown) and add a CAPTCHA/turnstile if abuse appears.
- **Log consent text version** if the wording may change (add `consent_version` column).

Let me know your stack (Express/Django/Rails/PHP), email provider (SendGrid/Mailgun/SES/Postmark), and whether you want double opt-in — I'll tailor the code.

